{
  "number": 10,
  "meaning": "Divine order, completeness, and legislation",
  "description": "The number ten represents divine order and completeness, particularly in relation to governance and legislation. God gave the Ten Commandments as the foundation for His covenant with His people and their guide for life. The ten plagues struck Egypt as an expression of God's complete judgment against idols. The tithe (one-tenth) was given back to God as recognition of His sovereignty over all creation. In Jesus' parable, the ten virgins represent the fullness of those waiting who prepare themselves for the bridegroom's coming.",
